    "media:imagetext": "EMERGENCY EXIT INFORMATION\nThe airplane on which you are traveling is one of the safest aircraft in service\ntoday.\nYour safety is always our first concern, and our pilots and flight\nattendants are thoroughly trained to cope with any emergency which might\nShould it ever be necessary to evacuate the aircraft, there are a number\nof exits available for your use. These are described below.\nWINDOW EXITS\nFRONT\nREAR\nWINDOW EXITS\nAUXILIARY\nCEILING EXIT\nRemove plastic\nshield. Turn\nhandle-clock-\nwise.\nPASSENGER\nDOOR EXIT\nDOOR EXITS\nEXID\nLift safety\nlatch, press\non red button,\nrotate door\nhandle counter\nclock-wise.\nPush window\nout and away\nfrom aircraft.\n(The forward\nright hand\nwindow extends\nto the floor)\nRemove plastic\nshield above\ndoor frame.\nTurn handle\ncounter clock-\nwise, push\nout top of\ndoor.\nEXIT\nFace forward,\nswing both\nfeet out,\njump to\nground.\nTop part of\ndoor falls\naway from\naircraft,\nlower part\nof door\ndrops down.\n1N1133344-1\nMove away from aircraft quickly\n(OVER)",
