    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "ALLEGHENY AIRLINES\nM298\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION\nSEAT BELTS\nPlease keep your seat belt fastened when the seat belt sign is on. When the seat\nbelt sign is turned off in flight, we suggest you keep your seat belt loosely fastened.\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC EQUIPMENT\nAM, FM, and TV receivers may not be used during the flight. These devices may\ndisturb the navigational aids of the aircraft.\nBRACE POSITION\n* Remove eyeglasses and sharp objects from pockets.\nFasten seat belt tight and low across your hips.\nFORWARD FACING SEATS\nREAR FACING SEATS\nIf there is a seat\nimmediately in front\nof you, place your\narms in crossed\nposition on back of\nseat in front of you.\nLean forward with your\nhead resting firmly\non your crossed arms.\nIf there is no seat\nimmediately in front\nof you, lean forward\nand down as far as\npossible. Clasp\nhands firmly under\nlegs.\nClasp hands firmly\nbehind head.\nLean back in seat.\nFLOTATION CUSHION\nYour seat cushion\nis designed to\nfloat.\nGrasp seat cushion\nand pull up.\nLeave aircraft.\nHold on to straps\nto keep afloat.\n(OVER)",
      "EMERGENCY EXIT INFORMATION\nThe airplane on which you are traveling is one of the safest aircraft in service\ntoday.\nYour safety is always our first concern, and our pilots and flight\nattendants are thoroughly trained to cope with any emergency which might\nShould it ever be necessary to evacuate the aircraft, there are a number\nof exits available for your use. These are described below.\nWINDOW EXITS\nFRONT\nREAR\nWINDOW EXITS\nAUXILIARY\nCEILING EXIT\nRemove plastic\nshield. Turn\nhandle-clock-\nwise.\nPASSENGER\nDOOR EXIT\nDOOR EXITS\nEXID\nLift safety\nlatch, press\non red button,\nrotate door\nhandle counter\nclock-wise.\nPush window\nout and away\nfrom aircraft.\n(The forward\nright hand\nwindow extends\nto the floor)\nRemove plastic\nshield above\ndoor frame.\nTurn handle\ncounter clock-\nwise, push\nout top of\ndoor.\nEXIT\nFace forward,\nswing both\nfeet out,\njump to\nground.\nTop part of\ndoor falls\naway from\naircraft,\nlower part\nof door\ndrops down.\n1N1133344-1\nMove away from aircraft quickly\n(OVER)"
    ],
